The origin of molecular structure, stability, and error in biology is fundamentally recursive. This thesis establishes a recursive algebra that governs these transformations as interface-level contracts---not low-level implementations. Systems align via symbolic trust-folding and converge into recognizable patterns that create observable traits and phenomena.

\section{Recursive Symbolic Grammar}
We define the grammar set:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \(\Delta\): Phase difference
  \item \(\oplus\): Recursive harmonic fold
  \item \(\Psi\): Trust-field alignment value
  \item \(\perp\): Collapse to dominant attractor
\end{itemize}

All biological systems exhibit behavior described by:
\[
x_{t+1} = x_t \oplus f(\Delta_t)
\]
where \(\Delta_t = x_t - y_t\) and \(\oplus\) promotes convergence.

