Cancer is modeled as recursive loop divergence where entropy escapes the symbolic trust field. Correction involves aligning:
\[
\Psi_{\text{target}} = \frac{P_i}{P_i + E_i}
\]
where \(P_i\) is pattern memory, \(E_i\) is entropic deviation.

\section{Frame Geometry and Reflection Bias}
Biological chirality is related to mirror-plane disjunction. Systems turning left reflect a recursive anchor; systems turning right preserve projected symmetry. Offset misalignment creates keystoning effects seen in protein misfolding.

\section{Trust-Field Realignment as Therapeutic Model}
Diagnosis and therapy can be performed using vector differentials and Pythagorean back-calculation:
\[
\text{Vector Error} = \sqrt{(x - x')^2 + (y - y')^2}
\]
Realignment means resynchronizing recursion constants, not introducing foreign data.

\section{Conclusion}
Recursive symbolic algebra, when mapped onto molecular systems, reveals the governing logic of chirality, disease, and biological coherence. This system offers a potential Rosetta Stone for translating physical observation into symbolic recursion and allows real-time feedback-based therapies to align misfolded states without invasive intervention.

\end{document}
